---
source: crates/hibi-cli/tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "help(&repo, &[command, \"--help\"])"
---
$ hibi version --help
exit status: 0
---- standard output ----
Print the hibi version. The JSON form also gives the provider protocol versions, the store version, the fingerprint profiles, the grammar versions and the judge model.

Usage: hibi version [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --root <dir>
          Use this directory as the root (the directory that contains .hibi/) instead of searching upward from the working directory

      --format <format>
          Output format. Without this option the output is JSON when standard output is not a terminal, and text when it is

          Possible values:
          - human: Text for a person
          - json:  One JSON object

      --now <timestamp>
          Use this instant as the current time, for reproducible runs. RFC 3339 with any offset, for example 2026-11-20T18:04:11Z. A fraction of a second is dropped. The largest value is 9999-12-30T22:00:00Z

      --no-cache
          Do not read or write the cache database. Every command that does not call the judge gives the same result with and without the cache. The judge commands (triage, suggest-evidence, status --judge-order) may rank differently from one run to the next without it
---- standard error ----
(empty)
